POSIX shim — INET client wire helpers + SCM_RIGHTS cmsg machinery
==================================================================

Same-module sibling of `shim.lsysl`. Owns the shim-side wire
helpers that talk to the inet server (INET_CMD_* request /
reply encoders) and the SCM_RIGHTS in-flight queued-ref
machinery — both the inet-side (`shim_inet_bump_oft_ref` etc.)
and the VFS-side (`shim_vfs_oft_queue_ref` etc.) helpers used
by sendmsg / recvmsg to keep cmsg fds alive while in transit.

Lifted out of `shim.lsysl` to keep that file focussed on the
per-process fd table + per-syscall handlers.

    module oskit.posix

    import oskit.ipc.{port_lookup, ipc_send}


INET client helpers (shim-side)
-------------------------------

Minimal wire helpers that mirror `oskit/servers/inet.lsysl`'s
message layout. The shim talks to the inet server via the same
IPC protocol that `oskit/net/client.lsysl` uses from user space;
we replicate the writers here instead of importing `oskit.net` to
keep the kernel link free of the full socket-API module.

